e  advocate for wild horses according to  the blm  as of march 2020 there were nearly 47  thousand wild horses in the state  that's more than half of all the wild  horses in the country  congresswoman titus and roy say they  support a method of birth control  through  darts for the animals advocates say it's  more cost effective and  more humane than roundups but so far the  blm  has shown resistance we've never come up  with somebody in the blm who really  cares about this and i think now  secretary holland will be the person who  can be a good partner  for us the i-team's request for an  interview with the new secretary of  interior who oversees the blm  was declined the american wild horse  campaign is now calling for an  investigation  into the adoption program it wants  employees held accountable  criminal prosecution for those who sold  the animals for slaughter  and for lawmakers to step in  congresswoman titus says  gradually there is more interest in  legislation  but there is also a challenge sometimes  it's hard to get through  the agriculture committee though because  it's so dominated  by ranching interests  congresswoman titus says she receives  the most amount of letters about this  issue people from all over the country  showing support for wild horses  even if they've never personally seen  one
 

